  "text": "Here is the implementation for the function `remove_adjacent_duplicates`:\n\n```python\nimport unittest\n\ndef remove_adjacent_duplicates(lst):\n    # Initialize a result list\n    result = []\n    \n    # Iterate through the input list\n    for item in lst:\n        # If the result list is empty or the current item is not the same as the last item in result\n        if not result or result[-1] != item:\n            result.append(item)\n    \n    return result\n\nclass TestRemoveAdjacentDuplicates(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_basic_functionality(self):\n        self.assertEqual(remove_adjacent_duplicates([1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4]), [1, 2, 3, 4])\n    \n    def test_repeated_elements(self):\n        self.assertEqual(remove_adjacent_duplicates([5, 5, 5, 6, 7, 7]), [5, 6, 7])\n    \n    def test_multiple_duplicates(self):\n        self.assertEqual(remove_adjacent_duplicates([1, 2, 3, 4, 4, 4, 4, 5, 5]), [1, 2, 3, 4, 5])\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    unittest.main()\n```\n\nThis code defines the `remove_adjacent_duplicates` function and includes unit tests to verify its correctness.",
